[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127580,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 240,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Plaque-like CD34-positive dermal fibroma is a benign tumour of fibroblastic origin characterized histologically by a band-like proliferation of bland CD34-positive spindle cells in the upper dermis, typically sparing the papillary dermis and adnexal structures.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T10:02:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127581,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 240,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8810/0 Plaque-like CD34-positive dermal fibroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T10:02:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127582,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 240,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B53.Y &amp; XH3665 Other specified fibroblastic or myofibroblastic tumour, primary site &amp; Plaque-like CD34-positive dermal fibroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T10:02:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127583,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 240,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> medallion-like dermal dendrocyte hamartoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T10:02:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127584,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 240,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T10:02:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127585,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 240,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour has a broad site distribution but shows a predilection for the proximal limbs, upper trunk, and neck {15337977; 20061935}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T10:02:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127586,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 240,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour typically presents as a solitary, slowly growing, asymptomatic, well-demarcated, round to oval or medallion-shaped, erythematous to brown-yellow plaque, or (less often) as a nodular or protuberant growth {26645569}, measuring several centimetres in diameter {15337977; 20061935}. The surface is often wrinkled, depressed, and pliable {20061935}. Some proliferations can be pruritic and painful {24003290}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T10:02:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127587,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 240,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour can be either a congenital or an acquired proliferation {15337977; 20061935; 30635930}. It has a wide age distribution but most commonly develops in children and young adults {15337977; 20061935; 28750558} and shows a female predominance {15337977; 20061935; 30635930}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T10:02:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127588,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 240,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T10:02:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127589,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 240,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T10:02:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127590,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 240,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T10:02:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127591,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 240,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour is distinguished by a band-like proliferation of variably cellular and fairly uniform fibroblasts in the upper and mid dermis, characteristically sparing the papillary dermis {15337977; 20061935}. Extension into the subcutaneous fatty tissue is rare {15337977; 20061935}. Some proliferations display a zonation pattern with perpendicular growth towards the surface and more storiform arrangements of tumour cells in the lower parts {20061935}. Concentric growth of tumour cells around adnexal structures, vascular channels, and nerves is often seen. The tumour cells are bland, with small nuclei, inconspicuous nucleoli, and rare mitoses {20061935}. Multiple dilated venules are present throughout the neoplasm {20061935}. Elastic fibres are often fragmented and reduced in number.</p>\r\n<h6>Immunohistochemistry</h6>\r\n<p>The tumour cells are diffusely positive for CD34 and fascin {15337977; 20061935; 30635930}. Staining for factor&nbsp;XIIIa is inconsistent.</p>\r\n<h6>Differential diagnosis</h6>\r\n<p>Plaque-like CD34 positive dermal fibroma must be distinguished from dermal dermatofibrosarcoma protuberans, dermatomyofibroma, and fibroblastic connective tissue naevus.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T10:02:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127592,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 240,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T10:02:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
